Z||000000||btoth||09-20-2000||10:25 AM||||a friend of mine just rebuilt the engine in his 85 gt.  he installed bosch +4 plugs and some high performance(?) wires durring the rebuild.  compression checks out and all vacuum lines are ok and the timming is dead on the 10 degree mark.  i figure that it has something to do with either the coil needing to be replaced (maybe it doesn't work well with the new wires and bosch plugs?) or maybe it would be best to try regular ac delco plugs before anything else...  any sugestions would be great!  TIA!  ~ brian||||reg||5
